<p class="meta"><span class="kicker">Work with me · English copy</span></p>
<h1>Korean beauty &amp; lifestyle product copy, <span class="mark">written for US shoppers</span></h1>
<p class="lead">If you sell Korean beauty or lifestyle products on Amazon, Shopify or your own store, I turn the Korean product description into English that reads naturally to US shoppers. I read the Korean source myself, draft with AI, and check every final sentence myself.</p>

<h2>What you get (per product)</h2>
<ul>
<li>A product title</li>
<li>5 bullet points</li>
<li>A short product description</li>
<li>How to use</li>
<li>The ingredient list in English names, exactly as printed on your package. I don't add or remove ingredients.</li>
<li>Notes on any phrases from the Korean source that I didn't carry over, and why</li>
</ul>

<h2>Pilot price</h2>
<div class="box">
<p class="price">$49 per product <span class="trial">Pilot price</span></p>
<p class="price">$199 for 5 products <span class="trial">Pilot price</span></p>
<p class="meta">One round of revisions is included. Payment is arranged by message after we agree on the scope. This site doesn't take payments.</p>
</div>

<h2>Samples</h2>
<p>All three samples below are fictional products I made up to show the style. The brand slot is left blank on purpose, and none of them is a real product.</p>

<div class="sample" lang="en"><span class="stamp">SAMPLE · fictional product</span>
<p class="meta">Skincare · Korean source (summary): 쌀겨 추출물이 들어간 약산성 젤 클렌저, 150ml. 거품이 부드럽고 세안 후 당기지 않음. 「피부 장벽 회복」. 아침·저녁 사용.</p>
<h3>[Brand] Low-pH Rice Bran Gel Cleanser, 150 ml / 5.07 fl oz</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Gentle daily gel cleanser:</b> A clear gel that turns into a soft, light lather with a little water.</li>
<li><b>Low-pH formula:</b> For morning and evening use.</li>
<li><b>Rice bran extract:</b> A classic Korean skincare ingredient, inspired by the traditional rice-water rinse.</li>
<li><b>No tight feeling:</b> Rinses off clean and leaves skin feeling soft, not stripped.</li>
<li><b>Easy-squeeze tube:</b> 150 ml / 5.07 fl oz.</li>
</ul>
<p>A gentle gel cleanser for every day. Work a small amount into a soft lather, massage over damp skin, and rinse. Skin feels clean and comfortable afterward.</p>
<p><b>How to use:</b> Wet your face. Lather a pea-sized amount with water in your palms, massage gently over your face, then rinse with lukewarm water. Use morning and evening.</p>
<p class="meta">What I changed: the Korean source said &ldquo;restores the skin barrier.&rdquo; That reads like a drug claim in the US, so I didn't carry it over and flagged it instead. Volume was converted from ml to fl oz.</p>
</div>

<div class="sample" lang="en"><span class="stamp">SAMPLE · fictional product</span>
<p class="meta">Body care · Korean source (summary): 무화과 향 핸드크림, 50ml, 끈적임 없이 빠르게 흡수, 가방에 넣기 좋은 크기. 「스트레스를 풀어 주는 향」.</p>
<h3>[Brand] Fig Leaf Hand Cream, 50 ml / 1.69 fl oz</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Soft fig leaf scent:</b> Green and lightly sweet, not heavy.</li>
<li><b>Non-greasy feel:</b> Absorbs quickly, so you can type or scroll right after applying.</li>
<li><b>Bag-sized tube:</b> 50 ml fits in a pocket, a tote or a desk drawer.</li>
<li><b>Light cream texture:</b> Spreads easily with a small amount.</li>
<li><b>Everyday use:</b> Apply whenever your hands feel dry.</li>
</ul>
<p>A light hand cream with a soft fig leaf scent. It sinks in fast and leaves hands feeling smooth, without a slippery film.</p>
<p><b>How to use:</b> Squeeze a small amount onto the back of your hand and smooth it over both hands and fingertips.</p>
<p class="meta">What I changed: the Korean source said the scent &ldquo;relieves stress.&rdquo; I described the scent itself instead of claiming an effect.</p>
</div>

<div class="sample" lang="en"><span class="stamp">SAMPLE · fictional product</span>
<p class="meta">Lifestyle · Korean source (summary): 스테인리스 수저 세트(숟가락 1·젓가락 1), 납작한 젓가락, 식기세척기 사용 가능, 선물 상자 포장.</p>
<h3>[Brand] Korean Stainless Steel Spoon &amp; Chopstick Set (Sujeo), Gift Boxed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>The Korean table set:</b> One long-handled spoon and one pair of chopsticks, called <i>sujeo</i> in Korean.</li>
<li><b>Flat chopsticks:</b> The flat shape is traditional in Korea and doesn't roll off the table.</li>
<li><b>Stainless steel:</b> Easy to wipe clean.</li>
<li><b>Dishwasher safe:</b> Or simply wash by hand with warm, soapy water.</li>
<li><b>Gift boxed:</b> Arrives in a box, ready to give.</li>
</ul>
<p>The spoon-and-chopsticks pair you'll find on almost every Korean table. A practical set for everyday meals, and an easy gift for anyone who loves Korean food.</p>
<p><b>Care:</b> Dishwasher safe. Dry after washing to keep the finish bright.</p>
<p class="meta">What I changed: I explained what <i>sujeo</i> is and why the chopsticks are flat, because US shoppers may not know. The Korean source didn't need that.</p>
</div>

<h2>How it works</h2>
<ol class="steps">
<li>Send a request through the &ldquo;Business proposal&rdquo; (비즈니스 제안) button on my link page. Tell me where the product page or the Korean description is.</li>
<li>I confirm that you have the rights to the product description.</li>
<li>I write one product first so we can agree on the tone.</li>
<li>I write the rest and check every final sentence myself.</li>
<li>You get one round of revisions. You publish the copy yourself.</li>
</ol>

<h2>What I don't do</h2>
<ul class="nots">
<li>Guarantee sales, rankings or search placement</li>
<li>Effect claims that make a cosmetic sound like a drug (&ldquo;treats,&rdquo; &ldquo;heals,&rdquo; &ldquo;cures&rdquo;). If they are in the Korean source, I don't carry them over and I tell you.</li>
<li>Copy for medical devices, drugs or dietary supplements</li>
<li>Regulatory or legal judgments. Registration, labeling, safety substantiation and FDA / MoCRA compliance stay the seller's responsibility.</li>
</ul>

